## 7. ThreeRuntime (3D path)

**Files:** `src/lib/three-engine/ThreeRuntime.ts`, `ThreeWorld.ts`, `src/lib/three-games/quiz-room/QuizRoom3DGame.ts`

1. `ThreeWorld.init(mount)` — Scene, PerspectiveCamera, WebGLRenderer (pixel ratio ≤ 1.75)
2. `GameSession.init(config)` — same managers as Pixi, RuleEngine last
3. `await game.init()` (QuizDataSource + procedural scene + raycast)
4. Emit `ENGINE_READY_FOR_GAME` (after the 3D game is ready so a failed quiz fetch does not start music)
5. `start()` — `game.start()` + one `requestAnimationFrame` loop
6. HUD `GAME_PAUSED` / `GAME_RESUMED` pause timers and the game
7. Destroy: cancel RAF → game → session → world (including `disposeObject3D` and context loss)

3D games emit `GAME_EVENTS.ANSWER_SELECTED` and `GAME_STATE_EVENTS.GAME_ENDED`. They never subclass `BaseGame` or call `scoringManager.addScore`.

